.TH LINTWRIGHT 1 "2026-10-18" "lintwright 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lintwright \- static analysis for Debian source packages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lintwright
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lintwright
reads a Debian source tree and reports the policy details that break archive
uploads and slow down review: changelog trailers, source formats, debhelper
compatibility levels, install paths and maintainer scripts.
.PP
It never executes package code and never contacts the network.  Every finding
carries a file, a line number and a stable tag, so a pipeline can suppress a
single rule without suppressing a file.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B check \fIpath\fR
Analyse the source tree rooted at \fIpath\fR (default: the current directory).
.TP
.B rules
List every rule with its default severity and a one-line summary.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-format text|json
Output format.  JSON is stable and intended for CI consumption.
.TP
.B \-\-fail\-on error|warning|info|never
Lowest severity that produces exit status 1.  Default: \fBerror\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-only \fITAG\fR
Run only this tag.  May be repeated.
.TP
.B \-\-skip \fITAG\fR
Never run this tag.  May be repeated.
.TP
.B \-\-statistics
Print a per-tag count table to standard error.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable colour even when standard output is a terminal.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
No findings at or above the \fB\-\-fail\-on\fR threshold.
.TP
.B 1
At least one finding at or above the threshold.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error: bad path, unknown tag, unknown option.
.SH EXAMPLES
Check a tree and fail the build on warnings:
.PP
.nf
.RS
lintwright check . \-\-fail\-on warning
.RE
.fi
.PP
Produce JSON for a CI annotation step:
.PP
.nf
.RS
lintwright check . \-\-format json > lintwright.json
.RE
.fi
.PP
Ignore one rule while bringing a legacy package up to date:
.PP
.nf
.RS
lintwright check . \-\-skip watch\-missing
.RE
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I debian/control
Source and binary package metadata.
.TP
.I debian/changelog
Most recent entry, validated for header, urgency, signature and date.
.TP
.I debian/rules
Build entry point; checked for shebang and executability.
.TP
.I debian/source/format
Source package format.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lintian (1),
.BR dpkg\-buildpackage (1),
.BR debhelper (7)
.PP
Debian Policy Manual, https://www.debian.org/doc/debian-policy/
